{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 0, "start_seconds": 0.0, "end_seconds": 3.0399999618530273, "text": "There's this really weird pattern down the east coast of America.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 1, "start_seconds": 3.0399999618530273, "end_seconds": 8.239999771118164, "text": "23,000 oval-shaped depressions that reach from New Jersey all the way down to Florida.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 2, "start_seconds": 8.239999771118164, "end_seconds": 11.119999885559082, "text": "And most of them point this way, northwest.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 3, "start_seconds": 11.119999885559082, "end_seconds": 14.5600004196167, "text": "They're called Carolina Bays because most of them are found in the Carolinas.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 4, "start_seconds": 14.5600004196167, "end_seconds": 17.360000610351562, "text": "Kind of looks as if the Earth has been shot up with a machine gun.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 5, "start_seconds": 18.31999969482422, "end_seconds": 19.68000030517578, "text": "So what caused them?", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 6, "start_seconds": 19.68000030517578, "end_seconds": 22.31999969482422, "text": "Well, scientists used to think that they were formed from a meteor,", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 7, "start_seconds": 22.31999969482422, "end_seconds": 27.360000610351562, "text": "which exploded over North America, creating this huge array of craters.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 8, "start_seconds": 27.360000610351562, "end_seconds": 30.8799991607666, "text": "But when they actually looked inside of the bays, they couldn't find any meteorites.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 9, "start_seconds": 30.8799991607666, "end_seconds": 34.31999969482422, "text": "And it turns out that the bays didn't appear at the same time.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 10, "start_seconds": 34.31999969482422, "end_seconds": 38.2400016784668, "text": "The oldest were shaped around 100,000 years ago, and the youngest ones", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 11, "start_seconds": 38.2400016784668, "end_seconds": 43.36000061035156, "text": "only about 10,000 years ago, which just happens to be the same time as the last ice age.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 12, "start_seconds": 43.36000061035156, "end_seconds": 45.040000915527344, "text": "If you go up to North Alaska today,", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 13, "start_seconds": 45.040000915527344, "end_seconds": 47.7599983215332, "text": "you can see tons of lakes that have a very similar oval shape.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 14, "start_seconds": 47.7599983215332, "end_seconds": 52.720001220703125, "text": "And we know that this part of Alaska gets blasted by strong southwesterly winds.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 15, "start_seconds": 52.720001220703125, "end_seconds": 56.31999969482422, "text": "So scientists have measured how water moves inside these lakes.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 16, "start_seconds": 56.31999969482422, "end_seconds": 59.91999816894531, "text": "And they've shown that with these winds, it creates a circular current", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 17, "start_seconds": 59.91999816894531, "end_seconds": 62.47999954223633, "text": "that makes lakes erode faster around the edges.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 18, "start_seconds": 62.47999954223633, "end_seconds": 65.76000213623047, "text": "And over decades and centuries and possibly even millennia,", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 19, "start_seconds": 65.76000213623047, "end_seconds": 69.5999984741211, "text": "these slowly elongate perpendicular to the direction of the wind.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 20, "start_seconds": 69.5999984741211, "end_seconds": 71.5999984741211, "text": "But what they found was that in northern Alaska,", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 21, "start_seconds": 71.5999984741211, "end_seconds": 73.5199966430664, "text": "those bays had to be created from permafrost.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 22, "start_seconds": 73.5199966430664, "end_seconds": 75.19999694824219, "text": "So the Earth itself had to be frozen.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 23, "start_seconds": 75.19999694824219, "end_seconds": 78.4000015258789, "text": "And Carolina never got that cold, even during the last ice age.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 24, "start_seconds": 79.68000030517578, "end_seconds": 84.0, "text": "Yet it was still a harsh, extremely cold landscape, which had little plant cover.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 25, "start_seconds": 84.0, "end_seconds": 88.63999938964844, "text": "Without vegetation holding the sandy soil in place, it was easily shaped by strong winds.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 26, "start_seconds": 89.19999694824219, "end_seconds": 91.83999633789062, "text": "And with a massive ice sheet sitting just to the north,", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 27, "start_seconds": 91.83999633789062, "end_seconds": 93.83999633789062, "text": "well, there was this huge temperature contrast", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 28, "start_seconds": 93.83999633789062, "end_seconds": 96.63999938964844, "text": "that helped drive those winds down across the region.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 29, "start_seconds": 96.63999938964844, "end_seconds": 100.55999755859375, "text": "Scientists do believe that strong winds likely carved indents into the landscape", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 30, "start_seconds": 100.55999755859375, "end_seconds": 102.72000122070312, "text": "and that those allowed rainwater to fill them.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 31, "start_seconds": 102.72000122070312, "end_seconds": 105.5999984741211, "text": "And then you have the same impact that happened in Alaska.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 32, "start_seconds": 105.5999984741211, "end_seconds": 108.95999908447266, "text": "You get water that's swirling and getting pushed by a prevailing wind", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 33, "start_seconds": 108.95999908447266, "end_seconds": 111.68000030517578, "text": "and creating these indentations that spread over time.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 34, "start_seconds": 111.68000030517578, "end_seconds": 113.91999816894531, "text": "Many of these lakes have been filled in with sediment.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 35, "start_seconds": 114.0, "end_seconds": 116.23999786376953, "text": "Some have been destroyed by agriculture.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 36, "start_seconds": 116.23999786376953, "end_seconds": 119.68000030517578, "text": "But the ones that do remain are havens for crazy wildlife.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
{"video_id": "nMqWWO6p7-c", "segment_index": 37, "start_seconds": 119.68000030517578, "end_seconds": 123.68000030517578, "text": "In fact, the Carolina Bays are actually the native habitat of the Venus flytrap.", "transcription_model": "whisper-1"}
